    Then the product details should remain available with a review count of 0                                    # None
    And the reviews area should show an empty state or no review entries without fabricated reviews              # None
    And the rating should use the site empty-state presentation without NaN or division-by-zero errors           # None
    And the review-entry control should remain available                                                         # None

@F11
Feature: F11 - Update / Remove Cart # features/update_remove_cart.feature:4
  Update valid quantities, reject nonnumeric quantities, and remove the last item.
  Prerequisites that are unavailable must be reported as Blocked before execution.
  @F11
  Feature: F11 - Update / Remove Cart  # features/update_remove_cart.feature:4

  @TC-F11-01 @OP-F11-1 @valid
  Scenario: TC-F11-01 - Update cart quantity                                                                                           # features/update_remove_cart.feature:16
    Given I have an isolated cart session with one currency, no coupon or voucher, and no selected shipping service                    # None
    And I have added one unit of an available product with no required options, no quantity discount at 2 units, and stock for 2 units # None
    And I use iPhone product ID "40" if it meets these fixture conditions                                                              # None
    And the cart contains exactly one product line with quantity 1                                                                     # None
    And I have recorded the displayed unit price as U and any tax or fee rows using displayed currency precision                       # None
    When I open Shopping Cart and record the product, unit price, quantity, and totals                                                 # None
    And I change the quantity from 1 to 2 and select the line Update control                                                           # None
    Then the same single product line should show quantity 2 without a duplicate line                                                  # None
    And the line total should equal 2 times U                                                                                          # None
    And the subtotal should equal the sum of displayed line totals                                                                     # None
    And the grand total should reconcile with the subtotal and displayed tax, fee, and discount rows                                   # None
    When I refresh Shopping Cart                                                                                                       # None
    Then quantity 2 and the recalculated totals should persist                                                                         # None

  @TC-F11-02 @OP-F11-2 @invalid @requires_A2
  Scenario: TC-F11-02 - Submit a nonnumeric cart quantity                                                                                        # features/update_remove_cart.feature:30
    Given I have an isolated cart session with one currency, no coupon or voucher, and no selected shipping service                              # None
    And I have added one unit of an available product with no required options, no quantity discount at 2 units, and stock for 2 units           # None
    And I use iPhone product ID "40" if it meets these fixture conditions                                                                        # None
    And the cart contains exactly one product line with quantity 1                                                                               # None
    And I have recorded the displayed unit price as U and any tax or fee rows using displayed currency precision                                 # None
    Given acceptance assumption A2 that invalid quantity is rejected without removing the item or changing its valid quantity has been confirmed # None
    When I open Shopping Cart and record its original product, quantity, and totals                                                              # None
    And I attempt to replace quantity 1 with "abc"                                                                                               # None
    And I select Update if the field accepts the characters or record the visible input restriction                                              # None
    Then the field should prevent nonnumeric entry or a visible validation response should reject the submitted value                            # None
    When I refresh Shopping Cart                                                                                                                 # None
    Then the original product should remain at quantity 1 with its original line total, subtotal, and grand total                                # None
    And no invalid numeric values or server errors should appear                                                                                 # None

